.TH LINK "1" "2026-07-28" "BNU 9.11" "BNU Commands"
.SH NAME
link \- call the link function to create a link to a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B link
\fI\,FILE1 FILE2\/\fR
.br
.B link
\fI\,OPTION\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" This page is derived from GNU Coreutils documentation.
This page documents BNU, an independent Bun implementation compatible with
GNU Coreutils 9.11.
.PP
Call the link function to create a link named FILE2 to an existing FILE1.
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/link#link--help'\fB\-\-help\fP\X'tty: link'
display this help and exit
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/link#link--version'\fB\-\-version\fP\X'tty: link'
output version information and exit
